ed on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=20:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-20I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]-20[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & -19 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-20I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "14a251b8295654f53bb3e3a1b7ef561b3efb2a736f19545b21b1b6badaed7629"} {"question" "q-170412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The minimum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $-1.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-1)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "14a251b8295654f53bb3e3a1b7ef561b3efb2a736f19545b21b1b6badaed7629"} {"question" "q-170411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0