nding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-4I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "14a251b8295654f53bb3e3a1b7ef561b3efb2a736f19545b21b1b6badaed7629"} {"question" "q-170410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077353/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b6590b3eb9a5683d22e607ad4ea28e12a4a412ff4ffd0caa5b90d29e827a6bc"} {"question" "q-170410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] 